            "settings_text_10_1": "Installed product",
            "settings_text_10_2": "Product version:",
            "settings_text_10_3": "New features",
            "settings_text_10_4": "© 2025 QuickRapidX, Good Fox",
            "settings_text_10_5": "Code licensed under MIT, while the QuickRapidX logo is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.",
            "settings_text_10_6": "Github | Good Fox",
            "settings_text_10_0": "Open source",
            "settings_text_10_7": "Full-cycle engineer — from interface to server.",
            "settings_text_10_8": "16 years in development, 7 of them commercial. Takes a product whole: interface, server logic, database, infrastructure, deployment and defense — nine layers usually split between four people…",
            "settings_text_10_8_2": "16 years in development, 7 of them commercial. Takes a product whole: interface, server logic, database, server, domain, certificates, deployment and monitoring — nine layers usually split between four people. Works remotely in TypeScript, Rust, Python and Node.js, runs a personal Linux server fleet, and handles DDoS protection across layers L3–L7. A separate line of work is a cognitive engine of his own: not a wrapper around someone else's language model but an architecture designed from scratch. It keeps its own memory, shows the state of its core and learns mid-conversation, running on an ordinary CPU with no graphics card. Take apart, understand, rebuild better — that is the working method, which makes unfamiliar code and abandoned projects an ordinary task rather than an obstacle. QuickRapidX is built the same way, and it is open: from Windows system calls to the last button in the interface, the source is under MIT.",
            "about_core_title": "Cognitive core",
            "about_core_state_1": "memory · linking",
            "about_core_state_2": "imagination · recombining",
            "about_core_state_3": "world model · rebuilding",
            "about_core_state_4": "learning · mid-conversation",
            "about_core_text": "Not a language model. An architecture designed from scratch: associative thinking, mental and combinatorial modeling, recombination of memory. It keeps a memory of its own, shows the state of its core and learns mid-conversation — on an ordinary CPU, with no graphics card.",
            "about_core_wip": "In active development",
